cartridge "WORD GUESS/COMPUTE!'S GAZETTE/1984"

' WORD GUESS
' A ColecoVision game based on "WORD GUESS", COMPUTE!'s Gazette, December
' 1984 (Commodore 64 and VIC-20 + 8K BASIC; orig/word guess_64.bas and
' orig/word guess.bas, the same game). The listings carry no author REM
' and the disk names none. Made for Amy Studio by Claude (an AI made by
' Anthropic), 2026, in Amy by Amy Bienvenu.
'
' The game, as the listing plays it: a word of 3 to 10 letters is picked at
' random from 100 built-in words (lines 1000-1100) and shown as blank slots.
' You have the word's length plus 5 guesses; every guess counts, right or
' wrong. A letter that is in the word shows in every slot where it
' appears. You have 30 seconds for each guess (GT=30, line 9): the clock
' counts down once a second and starts again after each guess; when it
' runs out the guess is lost and a dash goes into the list of letters
' guessed (line 109). Fill every slot before the guesses run out to win
' ("CONGRATULATIONS"), else "SORRY, YOU MISSED THE WORD" and the word is
' shown. Either way the time taken, GUESS TIME m:ss, is shown: the
' listing's only score. A word is not given twice until all have been
' played (the WU flags, line 35).
'
' Kept from the listing: the 100 words in its order (EARTHQUAKE twice, as
' printed), the length + 5 guesses, the 30-second clock per guess and the
' dash for a lost guess, the guess list, the guess time, the high blip for
' a letter found and the long low tone for a lost word.
'
' Liberties:
' - Joystick, no typing (Amy's rule for word games): the letters A-Z are on
'   the screen in two rows of 13; the stick moves a box over them (left and
'   right step through A-Z and wrap from Z to A, up and down switch rows;
'   held, it repeats after 14 frames, then every 5), a button guesses the
'   letter under the box. Letters already guessed are greyed (green when
'   they were in the word) and can't be guessed again: the listing let you
'   type a letter twice and lost a guess for it.
' - RULES on the title (left/right): EASY, the default, or ORIGINAL (the
'   listing's rule unchanged). EASY: letters found are free, only misses
'   count, 8 allowed (MISSES LEFT on screen), and the word's first letter is
'   shown at the start in every slot where it appears; a guess lost to
'   the clock is a miss. Added because blind guessing wins about 7% under the listing's
'   length + 5 rule.
' - One word per game: after the word, the result and the guess time stay
'   until a button press, then the title (house rule, no F3/F5 question).
'   The title counts the words solved this session.
' - Line 35's "IF WU(RN)=1 THEN 110" jumped into the guess loop with the
'   last guess still in GS$ when it hit a word already played, and once all
'   100 had been played it looped for ever; here the next unplayed word is
'   taken, and after all 100 the list starts again.
' - The clock is shown as a number and a bar (one block per 2 seconds, red
'   in the last 5 seconds, a soft tick each of those seconds); a lost guess
'   gives a short noise. Original title tune "Spell It Out", played once.
'
' Controls: joystick and either button; keypad not used. Title: up/down
' choose START GAME, HOW TO PLAY or CREDITS, a button picks.
'
' House rules: text and tiles in columns 2-29, rows 1-22; tiles from code
' 128; screens drawn with the NMI off and the display off. Music first in
' the sound table, the title tune played once. `set sprite count` always
' given. Nothing flashes.

